                        "review": "Even on the lowest difficulty you're only 'allowed' to be in first place for 1-3 seconds before the NPC's get massive increases their base (non-boost) speed and pass you. In order to finish in first the best strategy seems to be staying in 3th - 5th place while hoarding your boosts for the entire race, then unloading the boosts near the finish line to win.\n\nNice aesthetics, but the excessive rubber banding sucks all the fun out of it.",
